  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when you've put in all that effort installing window casing, only for it to just not look quite right. One of the biggest culprits is inaccurate measurements. Even a small miscalculation can throw off the whole look, especially when it comes to mitered corners. Another common issue is poor alignment – if your pieces aren't perfectly straight and flush with the window jamb and wall, you'll end up with noticeable gaps or an uneven appearance. Sometimes people skip critical finishing steps like filling nail holes or caulking, which leaves the casing looking unfinished and exposes imperfections. And hey, not test-fitting those miter joints before you nail them in is a classic mistake. You want to make sure they're snug and seamless! If you're finding yourself wrestling with these problems or dealing with complex openings, it might be time to call in a professional. HH Remodeling LLC specializes in detailed interior finish work, and we can make sure your window casing looks flawless and really elevates your space. We're happy to chat about your project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}